  {
   "id": 242218,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<p><img src=\"exercises/media/f2edaf9efdd94d32.jpg\" alt=\"Solution A contains shriveled red blood cells. Solution B contains bloated red blood cells. One of the bloated cells has burst.\"></p>\n\n<p>The diagram shows red blood cells in two different NaCl solutions. What is likely causing the cells to differ in shape in the two solutions?</p>\n",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 758335,
     "content_html": "Solution A has high osmolarity. Solution B has low osmolarity."
    },
    {
     "id": 758332,
     "content_html": "Solution A has low osmolarity. Solution B high osmolarity."
    },
    {
     "id": 758333,
     "content_html": "The cells in solution A are osmoregulators. The cells in solution B are osmoconformers."
    },
    {
     "id": 758334,
     "content_html": "The cells in solution A are osmoconformers. The cells in solution B are osmoregulators."
    }
   ],
